    "reducedMotion": "No frame loop is opened. One frame is drawn at `uElapsed = 0.4`, which shows both cylinders at a legible yaw with the first note group lit, so the structure and the highlight convention are both visible. Neither the rotation nor the playhead advances.",
    "cleanup": "Nulls the stage ref so a queued frame cannot touch a dead renderer, disposes the geometry through `disposeObject(scene)`, disposes the material, calls `disposeRenderer` for `dispose` + `forceContextLoss` + a zeroed backing store, and removes the canvas. `useRaf` unsubscribes on unmount.",
    "acceptance": "Two stacked cylinders of dots turn at a constant rate, showing different faces to the viewer. Dots on the far side are visibly smaller and dimmer than those on the near side, and no dot ever pops in front of one it should be behind. A cluster of larger note dots lights every 1.2 seconds and cycles around the cylinder. Resize the container and the piece rescales without a flicker. With reduced motion it holds a single legible frame.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical",
