    "reducedMotion": "No frame loop is opened. A single frame is drawn at `uElapsed = 1.9` — past the one-second amplitude ramp, and a third of the way through the default cycle, so the crest sits inside the lattice rather than off its edge. Both the depth falloff and the wave band are visible in that still; neither advances.",
    "cleanup": "Nulls the stage ref so a queued frame cannot touch a dead renderer, disposes the geometry through `disposeObject(scene)`, disposes the material, calls `disposeRenderer` for `dispose` + `forceContextLoss` + a zeroed backing store, and removes the canvas. `useRaf` unsubscribes on unmount, so a StrictMode double-invoke leaves no orphaned context.",
    "acceptance": "A curved lattice of dots is visibly dimmer and smaller toward its left and right edges than at its centre. A band of brighter, larger dots sweeps repeatedly across the field, roughly once every three seconds, rather than the whole field brightening at once. The lattice rocks gently side to side. Nothing flashes on mount. Resize the container and the field rescales without a flicker or a dropped context. With reduced motion it holds a single frame showing both the depth falloff and the crest.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical",
