    "reducedMotion": "Nothing in this component moves in either state — there is no animation, transition or timer to disable. The surface renders identically with `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` set, including the fold and the edge fade.",
    "cleanup": "Nothing to clean up. No listeners, no timers, no animation frames. The hoisted `<style>` is reference-counted by React and removed when the last instance unmounts.",
    "acceptance": "The dot grid is crisp at 100% and at 150% browser zoom — individual dots stay round, not square. All four edges dissolve rather than ending on a line, and the interior is perfectly even. With `scrollable` and `attachment=\"local\"`, scrolling the panel moves the dots with the text; with `attachment=\"scroll\"` the dots stay put while the text slides over them. With `fold`, the corner reads as turned paper with a single sharp crease and no blur.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical",
