    "reducedMotion": "Dragging is unchanged — it is the user's own motion, and tracking it is the component. Everything the component would have animated by itself is dropped: the idle drift is never registered on the ticker, the follow tween is never created (so the row is written straight to the wrapped position, one-to-one with the pointer, and a release does not throw), and the scatter timeline is not built, so pressing moves nothing but the row. Arrow keys still step one tile, instantly.",
    "cleanup": "Removes `pointerdown`, `pointermove`, `pointerup`, `pointercancel`, `lostpointercapture`, the capture-phase `click` and `keydown`; releases pointer capture if a gesture is still live at unmount; removes the drift callback from `gsap.ticker`; kills the tweens on the proxy object so an in-flight throw cannot call `onUpdate` against a detached track; and reverts the `gsap.context` holding the scatter timeline, which also restores the tiles' inline transforms. Both shared resize observers and the shared intersection observer unregister.",
    "acceptance": "The row drifts on its own. Grab it and it follows your hand exactly, with no creep in the drift direction, and the cards tilt and shrink apart the instant you press — then settle back when you let go. Flick and release: it coasts on at the speed you left, slows, and rejoins the drift with no visible seam or jump. Drag several screens' worth in one fast swipe and the tiles stay in order — nothing teleports. Watch one tile go off the left edge and it reappears on the right at the same spacing as every other gap. Release the pointer outside the browser window and the row keeps drifting instead of freezing scattered. Release over a card and no click reaches it; tap without moving and it does. Resize the container narrower and wider — the seam never appears. Scroll it out of view and the drift stops until it is back.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical",
    "registryDependencies": [
      "damp",
      "prng",
      "use-gsap",
      "use-in-view",
      "use-reduced-motion",
      "use-resize-observer",
      "wrap"
    ]
