    "reducedMotion": "The only motion is the 200ms surface change when a card is selected; it carries `motion-reduce:transition-none`, so under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` the selection switches instantly.",
    "cleanup": "Nothing to clean up. The component has no timers, listeners or effects.",
    "acceptance": "Four cards show Total balance $84,230 +3.2%, Income $18,420 +6.1%, Expenses $9,140 +2.4% and Savings $32,400 +8.4%. The Expenses chip and sparkline are rose, the others lime. Each sparkline ends in a dot at its last value. Clicking Income sets aria-pressed on it, lifts it to a white surface and the demo caption reads \"Charting Income\". The row shows four cards across at 1100px, two at medium widths and, at 360px, one compact single-line card per row so all four plus the caption stay on screen. Light and dark both read correctly.",
