    "reducedMotion": "The reduced branch adopts the target scalars outright and lays the row out once, so the resolved geometry is on screen rather than a fast spread toward it. The frame loop is not subscribed at all, so no work is scheduled for a user who asked for none, and a later prop change still re-derives the layout immediately through the same code path. Because the layout is a pure function of the four scalars, the reduced render is pixel-identical to the settled animated one.",
    "cleanup": "`useRaf` unsubscribes from the shared loop on unmount and cancels the frame when it is the last subscriber; `useResizeObserver` and `useInView` remove their targets from their shared observers. No listeners, timers or tweens are created directly. Inline transforms are written only to elements this component owns and rendered, so they are removed with them.",
    "acceptance": "Set `bow` to 0 and the leftmost and rightmost item centres sit exactly on the edges of the box — resize the panel from narrow to wide and they stay there, with no jump and no breakpoint. Restore the bow and the outer items recede and shrink while their horizontal positions do not move. Raise the field of view and the row spreads on a smooth dolly rather than snapping. Item counts of 1 and 2 both render without a divide-by-zero or a NaN transform. With reduced motion on, the row is at its final geometry on first paint and the profiler shows no animation frames for it.",
