    "reducedMotion": "The idle drift is set to zero, so the ring holds still and the same card stays in focus. Layout changes still happen — refusing them would leave the component unable to answer its own prop — but the parameters are assigned rather than tweened, so the new arrangement is simply there on the next frame with nothing travelling across the screen. The frame loop keeps running only because it is what draws; with no drift and no tween it writes the same transforms every frame.",
    "cleanup": "Kills the parameter tween (and any tween of the same object) so GSAP cannot write into a vector nothing reads; removes every mesh from the scene, then `disposeObject` for the materials, `geometry.dispose()`, `prototype.dispose()`, and `disposeRenderer` — which stops the animation loop, disposes, calls `forceContextLoss()` and zeroes the backing store — before removing the canvas from the DOM. The shared rAF unsubscribes, and the shared resize, intersection and visibility observers all unregister. No textures are allocated, so there are none to leak.",
    "acceptance": "The cards turn slowly and endlessly — watch one leave the bottom of the drum and come back at the top, at the same spacing. Switch layout: the whole formation unwinds into a row, or collapses into a stack, in one continuous motion, and at every instant it looks like a formation rather than cards travelling to new addresses. Nothing passes through the centre of the drum on the way. Switch layout twice quickly and the second morph starts from wherever the first had reached, with no jump. In the stack, the overlap order is stable while it drifts — nothing flickers in front of its neighbour. Resize the window from narrow to wide: the row still spans the frame and the cards keep their proportions. Scroll the canvas out of view and the GPU goes quiet.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical",
