    "reducedMotion": "The bar rebalance and the dimming transitions carry `motion-reduce:transition-none`, so under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` the bar and tiles jump straight to their new state.",
    "cleanup": "Nothing to clean up. The component has no timers, listeners outside React or effects.",
    "acceptance": "The headline equals the sum of shown values and the bar segments are proportional to them. The tile percents add up to 100. Clicking a tile hides its series: its percent reads \"Off\", its dot becomes a ring, its bar segment collapses and the total drops. Clicking it again restores it. The last shown tile cannot be hidden. Hovering a tile dims the other segments. Tiles sit two per row on narrow cards and four per row on wide ones. Light and dark both read correctly.",
