    "reducedMotion": "The panel's scale and blur are behind `motion-safe:` and are dropped under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; the backdrop and panel still fade over 300ms, so opening and closing remain perceptible without movement.",
    "cleanup": "React Aria releases the focus trap, restores focus to the trigger, and removes the scroll lock when the overlay unmounts after its exit transition. The ModalHeader layout effect resets the `described` flag on unmount. No timers or listeners of its own.",
    "acceptance": "Pressing \"Invite teammates\" fades in a dimmed backdrop and a panel that grows from slightly smaller and blurred to sharp; Tab cycles only inside the panel, Escape or a click on the backdrop closes it with the reverse animation, and focus returns to the trigger. In the delete AlertDialog, focus starts on Cancel, a backdrop click does nothing, and Delete shows a spinner with \"Deleting…\" while Cancel is disabled, then closes when the promise resolves.",
