    "reducedMotion": "No timeline is built at all. The counter is written straight to 100, the last word is set, the component unmounts itself and `onDone` fires on the same tick — so a reduced-motion visitor sees the real page immediately rather than a silent panel that still has to be waited out.",
    "cleanup": "`useGsap` runs the whole build inside a `gsap.context` scoped to the root and calls `ctx.revert()` on unmount, which kills the counter tween, the positioned `set` calls and the panel stagger, and restores every property they touched — including the span's original `textContent`.",
    "acceptance": "The number counts 000 to 100 with a visible ease, never changing width. Five words swap under it at even intervals and the last word lands as the number does. The content lifts away and five columns retract upward in sequence, the wipe starting before the content has finished leaving. `onDone` fires once, after the last column. With reduced motion the preloader is gone on the first frame. Unmount mid-count and no transforms or altered text remain.",
