    "reducedMotion": "The fill is set to `scaleY: 1` and every entry to full opacity and scale during the first effect, with no triggers created. The spine renders as a completed timeline — the rule is drawn, every entry is emphasised, and nothing changes with scroll.",
    "cleanup": "`useGsap` reverts the `gsap.context`, killing the fill tween, all per-entry tweens and all of their ScrollTriggers, and restoring the inline transform and opacity. This matters more than usual here because the alternation flip rebuilds every trigger on resize: a surviving trigger would keep writing a right-edge `transform-origin` to a card now laid out on the left.",
    "acceptance": "Scroll down: the accent rule fills from the top and each entry brightens and grows outward from its own side of the rule as it arrives. Scroll back up and each entry dims again as it leaves the top, and the rule retreats. Stop mid-section and the fill continues for about half a second. Disable JavaScript and every entry is still readable at half opacity. Narrow the container and the entries stack to the right of a left-hand rule.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical",
