    "reducedMotion": "Not handled. The rail width, label blur, search field and popover transitions run at full duration under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, and none of the three files uses `motion-reduce:` variants. The motion is short (150 to 300ms) and never loops, but to honour the setting add `motion-reduce:transition-none` to the aside, `Collapsible` and the two popovers. The theme toggle, when shown, already skips its view-transition reveal under reduced motion.",
    "cleanup": "Every listener is scoped to an effect: the window `keydown` for ⌘L (always), the document `click` for outside-click (only while search is active) and the rAF that focuses the search input (cancelled if search closes first). Each is removed on unmount or when its condition ends. The account menu removes its `matchMedia` change listener, and the team menu reads the same query through `useSyncExternalStore`, which unsubscribes itself. React Aria tears down the popovers' focus scope and dismiss handlers when they close.",
    "acceptance": "The sidebar fills the page height beside the content, with Home selected and its 152 badge. Clicking the fold icon narrows the panel to a 60px rail as labels, badges and the ⌘L hint blur away, and the icons do not move sideways. Clicking it again restores everything. Pressing ⌘L or Ctrl+L, or clicking Quick Search, opens a ringed search field (expanding the rail if needed). Typing filters the rows, \"zzz\" shows \"No results\", and Escape or a click outside closes it. Clicking the Jordan Lee trigger opens an account list to the right that blurs and scales in, and clicking the Acme team card opens the team menu to the right, aligned with the card's bottom edge. Escape closes either. Settings opens the settings dialog, which is closed until then.",
