    "reducedMotion": "The thumb follows the pointer directly, with no tween, so dragging is the same under any setting. The hover and drag scale, shadow and bubble lift are 150ms CSS transitions of a few pixels. They are kept under `prefers-reduced-motion` because they report state, and `motion-reduce:transition-none` on the root removes them.",
