    "acceptance": "The card shows \"Visitors\", \"2,500\", a lime \"+5.2%\" chip and a \"Last 7 days\" select. Under it is a half gauge with lime, blue, purple and pink segments (Desktop, Mobile, Tablet, TV) separated by small gaps, with \"47%\" over \"Desktop\" in the centre, and four tiles: Desktop 1,180, Mobile 620, Tablet 380 and TV 320. Hovering the Mobile tile fades the other segments and tiles, the header reads \"Mobile\", \"620\" and \"25% of total\", and the centre reads \"25%\" over \"Mobile\". In the Needle look the needle and a lime arc point at 47%, \"0%\" and \"100%\" sit under the arc ends, and picking Mobile swings the needle back to 25%. \"Last 30 days\" re-proportions the segments, and the headline counts to 10,000.",
