    "reducedMotion": "When `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` matches, one pass clears every transform and the loop then writes nothing at all. The cards keep their layout, spacing and hover states, so the grid is intact — it simply does not flex. Toggling the OS setting takes effect on the next frame without a reload.",
    "cleanup": "`useRaf` unsubscribes from the shared loop on unmount, and `useScrollVelocity` does the same. There are no listeners, observers or timers to remove; the only state is refs and one element resolved after mount, and every transform is written on nodes React owns.",
    "acceptance": "A fast flick skews and stretches the cards in the direction of travel by different amounts per column, and they settle within about a third of a second after the scroll stops, with no overshoot. Text stays readable throughout. At rest, a paint-flashing or style-recalc profile shows no per-frame work. The settle takes the same wall-clock time at 60 and 144 Hz. With reduced motion on, nothing deforms.",
